&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Backend Engineer to join our Source Code Experience team within GitLab&#39;s Create stage. You&#39;ll help make everyday source code workflows clear, reliable, and efficient for people working across GitLab projects. As artificial intelligence agents increasingly write and manage code alongside people, you&#39;ll build backend capabilities and interfaces that support trustworthy collaboration between people and agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work in one of GitLab&#39;s oldest and most complex product areas, using Ruby and GraphQL to improve critical source code experiences across GitLab.com, self-managed instances, and GitLab Dedicated. The Source Code group is responsible for the backend and frontend aspects of the product categories within Source Code. With support from experienced team members, you&#39;ll help maintain high reliability through performance and structured query language tuning, caching, rate limiting, testing, observability, and resiliency. You&#39;ll collaborate with product management, product design, testing, security, user experience research, technical writing, Gitaly, Code Review, and other Source Code teams to deliver reliable and performant systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about the &lt;a class=&quot;textLink&quot; href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/devops/create/source-code/&quot;&gt;Create:Source Code teams&lt;/a&gt; in the GitLab Handbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Develop secure, well-tested, performant features and improvements using Ruby and GraphQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Work through complex requirements and legacy constraints to deliver clear solutions while protecting the reliability of this critical system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Design and maintain backend services, application programming interfaces, data models, and business logic that support intuitive source code workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Collaborate across functions and teams, both asynchronously and synchronously, and involve domain experts when their input will improve the outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Use artificial intelligence agents for well-scoped work when they can speed up delivery without sacrificing quality, and critically review their output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Write maintainable code that follows GitLab&#39;s standards and contribute to constructive code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Help strengthen reliability by monitoring production health metrics, participating in Tier 2 on-call, troubleshooting incidents, contributing to root cause analysis, and improving observability and resiliency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Share knowledge through code review, technical documentation, and everyday collaboration while learning from others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Professional experience building backend web applications, services, or application programming interfaces, with experience using Ruby and GraphQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;An understanding of relational databases, structured query language, data modeling, caching, background processing, and backend performance practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Experience contributing to user-facing workflows and maintaining their underlying systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Experience writing backend unit and integration tests, with familiarity with the testing pyramid, Git, and collaborative code review processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Experience using artificial intelligence coding agents and reviewing their output, or an interest in building these skills in a complex monorepo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Clear written and spoken English communication skills, including sharing useful status updates in a remote, asynchronous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;The ability to manage assigned priorities, work through ambiguity, take ownership of your work, and seek guidance when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work on a complex product area that serves GitLab.com, self-managed instances, and GitLab Dedicated. You&#39;ll work closely with Code Review, Gitaly, and other Source Code teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome candidates with different levels and types of experience. Many successful candidates don&#39;t meet every requirement. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiting team to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced Sr Manager, Technical Program Management to lead a team of TPMs in our Engineering org. Our R&amp;amp;D PMO is a new team within GitLab Engineering, so this is a great opportunity to help build out a new function and define the future of Program Management at GitLab.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This individual will be responsible for leading a team of TPMs of varying levels, all working on different areas of the Product. The Sr. Manager, Technical Program Management will work closely with Product and Engineering leadership to ensure that TPMs are assigned to high priority programs and that they are successfully delivering results for customers. In addition to managing a team, this leadership position will also contribute to the long-term operational success of the R&amp;amp;D organization by partnering with leaders to develop new planning cadences and other improvements to our ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for directly GitLab team members performing in the role of Technical Program Manager. Lead and mentor a team of Technical Program Managers, including providing regular feedback to foster their growth and ensure their success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for staffing requirements for the PMO, in partnership with the Director of Technical Program Management and the Product and engineering Leadership groups. Align TPM team resourcing / assignments with the company’s business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain program management standards for elements including program documentation, project plans, status reports, post-mortems as well as a team direction north star; work to continuously improve and iterate on these processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain a long-term strategy and vision for the Program Management function, in alignment with broader company goals. Develop and expand upon the job family, CDF, and long-term hiring and growth objectives for the Technical Program Management function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships&amp;nbsp; with cross-functional stakeholders including Engineering, Product, Security, and GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and mitigate risks, resolve conflicts, and remove obstacles for the Technical Program Management team to ensure timely program delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and track key performance indicators (KPIs) for programs and team members and hold the team accountable for meeting commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic planning with direct influence over staffing decisions, project timelines, and planning stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate leadership as expected of Managers across GitLab and Embody our&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/values/#:~:text=values%20at%20GitLab-,CREDIT,other%20by%20assuming%20good%20intent.&quot;&gt; CREDIT values&lt;/a&gt; in your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as a people manager and as an IC TPM, ideally in a position of seniority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and delegate work effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of successful collaboration with internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing on strategic team development plans&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to coach others on driving cross functional product-driven initiatives, without direct control of the programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to position oneself and the team as trusted partners and thought leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/job-families/engineering/technical-program-management/#senior-manager-technical-program-management&quot;&gt;More information about the Sr Manager Job Family is available in our handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Technical Program Management function is relatively new to GitLab; we are building out a PMO that is centralized within Engineering and looking for strong TPMs that are interested in developing a newly formed PMO and standardizing on best practices for the business.&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/product-development/r-and-d-pmo/&quot;&gt; You can learn more about the PMO in our handbook page.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/stock-options/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLequity&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;equity&lt;/a&gt;. Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;United States Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ready to shape the future of talent acquisition in a global trading firm? As a Senior Campus Recruiter, you&#39;ll be the driving force behind spotting and bringing the top 1% of talent from Europe&#39;s premier universities on board. Your journey involves navigating the full campus recruitment lifecycle, from identification to selection, and making your mark at European recruitment events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll join our Campus Recruitment team in Europe, based in Amsterdam, part of a wider recruitment organisation of experienced tech, trading and business support recruiters. Collaboration comes first here: we share knowledge, step in for each other in peak season, and succeed as one team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end recruitment process: screening, interviewing, assessment review, offer conversations and closing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong partnerships with business leaders and interviewers, and make sure we&#39;re aligned on hiring needs and on what great looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a data-driven way, using insights to make our process sharper, fairer and more efficient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to strategic projects such as market analyses, process and assessment reviews, and improvements to how we select&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent IMC at recruitment events across Europe, with frequent travel (more than four times a year)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of industry experience, ideally within a global finance, trading, tech or consultancy organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of financial markets and the trading industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A critical eye: you question how things are done, spot trends early and turn them into practical improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to think strategically and act tactically, moving easily between the bigger picture and getting things done today&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solution-oriented mindset: when something isn&#39;t working, you look for a better way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy operational recruitment. Running a tight process and giving candidates a great experience energises you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build relationships with the business with ease and earn trust as a partner, not just a service provider&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in a dynamic environment where no two days are the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well in a larger team and put collaboration first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You keep up with industry trends and best practices in campus recruitment and bring them into your own work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A unique work culture that values collaboration, initiative, and ownership. Our professional and friendly environment provides the perfect backdrop for your growth and responsibilities. We operate with transparency in a flat structure, allowing you direct engagement with stakeholders and professionals. Your input matters here, contributing to our collective success. At IMC, continuous learning is a priority. Various training and on-the-job growth opportunities allow you to shape your path within the organisation. This isn&#39;t just a job; it&#39;s a journey of ongoing growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We appreciate your efforts. Our highly competitive salary comes with great perks. If you&#39;re looking for a friendly yet professional space to contribute and grow, IMC is the place. If you&#39;re ready for a role beyond routine recruitment, where your experience can contribute to the future of our team and company, apply now.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;IMC is a research-driven trading firm where quantitative modeling, machine learning, and engineering shape how modern markets are traded. A stabilizing force in markets since 1989, we provide liquidity across trading venues, delivering the best outcome in value and risk management to investors. Using our own technology and capital, we build proprietary systems and algorithms that operate across global markets. Our researchers, traders, and engineers work as a collective, combining rapid experimentation, advanced infrastructure, and real-time feedback to turn insight into execution and execution into advantage.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Are you comfortable navigating complex software systems, working with coding agents, and defining what makes developer tools actually useful? Do you want to shape how developers and AI work together inside IDEs?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About JetBrains&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create intelligent software development tools for developers and teams. More than 15 million users, over 300,000 companies, and 88 of the Fortune Global Top 100 rely on our products to solve real, complex problems. Our mission is simple: make development teams more productive and AI adoptable at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agentic development is changing how software gets built. Developers no longer just chat with AI – they delegate tasks, run parallel agent sessions, and steer autonomous changes. As agents take on more work, reviewing and owning the output is becoming the hardest part of the process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JetBrains Air is our open system for agentic development. It brings tools like Codex, GitHub Copilot, Claude Agent, Gemini, and Junie directly into JetBrains IDEs, providing an agentic-first user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Product Manager to lead key areas of Air. You’ll take ownership of high-impact workflows, work closely with cross-functional teams (including software engineers, designers, ML researchers, analysts, DevRel, and product marketing), and turn technical complexity into clear product direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end ownership of key parts of Air in JetBrains IDEs, driving work from problem framing and discovery to delivery, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and refine core agentic workflows, including task delegation, session monitoring, steering, and code review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model complex user flows, system states, permissions, and integration schemes to guide engineering and design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a transparent roadmap that balances quick improvements with long-term strategic investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define telemetry, design experiments, analyze product data, and make evidence-based roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Study how developers interact with leading AI agents and tools to inform product priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with the Agent Client Protocol (ACP) ecosystem and collaborate with partners building on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with enterprise sales and support teams to address governance, privacy, and control requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems-thinking mindset that easily breaks down complex architectures, workflows, and dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven approach to product decisions, including hands-on experience querying and analyzing telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active personal experience using coding agents and clear perspectives on where current AI tools succeed and fail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product intuition for complex technical user experiences and developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise, and collaborative communication skills with the ability to explain complex technical concepts simply and build alignment across diverse groups of stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort navigating fast-changing technical landscapes with high ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience shipping end-user products as a product manager or in a similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical grounding in software development workflows, including IDEs, git, code review, CI/CD, and package management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on technical background sufficient to collaborate closely with software and ML engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of core AI and agent concepts, including tool use, protocols (MCP/ACP), context retrieval, evaluations, and latency/cost trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to write SQL or Python to analyze product metrics and experiment results independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English, both written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first 6 to 12 months, success in this role means:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving measurable growth in active Air users and improving weekly/monthly retention (D7/D30).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increasing agent session completion rates and the proportion of agent-generated changes accepted by developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishing clear, telemetry-backed decisions across your product roadmap areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering validated product hypotheses consistently each quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing directly to JetBrains AI revenue growth and overall IDE value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join JetBrains?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong base salary – We offer competitive pay that reflects your skills and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
